From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:01:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 35/51] Let OBS's transform controls size the caption box

Scene items showing a captions source now use a bounding box (max size
only), and the source takes that box as its width and height, so
dragging the frame or typing a size in Edit Transform resizes the
caption box and re-wraps the text at its font size instead of scaling
it. Items scaled before (or reset) become a box of the same visible
size; width and height changed in the source's properties move the
items' boxes. Move, rotate, snap, crop and alignment stay OBS's own.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
